JsonSerializer.Serialize(writer, Error);
// TO:
JsonSerializer.Serialize(writer, Error, AzureResourceManagerSerializerContext.Default.ResponseError);
```

Line 173:
```csharp
// FROM:
array.Add(JsonSerializer.Deserialize<OperationStatusResult>(item.GetRawText()));
// TO:
array.Add(JsonSerializer.Deserialize(item.GetRawText(), AzureResourceManagerSerializerContext.Default.OperationStatusResult));
```

Line 184:
```csharp
// FROM:
error = JsonSerializer.Deserialize<ResponseError>(property.Value.GetRawText());
// TO:
error = JsonSerializer.Deserialize(property.Value.GetRawText(), AzureResourceManagerSerializerContext.Default.ResponseError);
```

### 5. All four LongRunningOperation files with `ToObjectFromJson`:
- `ManagementGroup/Generated/LongRunningOperation/ManagementGroupsArmOperation.cs` (line 61)
- `ManagementGroup/Generated/LongRunningOperation/ManagementGroupsArmOperationOfT.cs` (line 61)
- `Resources/Generated/LongRunningOperation/ResourcesArmOperation.cs` (line 61)
- `Resources/Generated/LongRunningOperation/ResourcesArmOperationOfT.cs` (line 61)

In each, change:
```csharp
// FROM:
var lroDetails = ModelReaderWriter.Write(rehydrationToken, ModelReaderWriterOptions.Json, AzureResourceManagerContext.Default).ToObjectFromJson<Dictionary<string, string>>();
// TO:
var lroDetails = JsonSerializer.Deserialize(ModelReaderWriter.Write(rehydrationToken, ModelReaderWriterOptions.Json, AzureResourceManagerContext.Default).ToString(), AzureResourceManagerSerializerContext.Default.DictionaryStringString);
```

Make sure to add `using System.Text.Json;` to those LongRunningOperation files if not already present.

